    "objective": "Supervise direct task execution end to end\n\nRF-10a: implement the direct golden path from approved state through safe pre-operations, EXECUTOR work order, observed receipt, evaluator, post-operations, and typed approval/wait/human stops.",
    "acceptance_criteria": [
      "bun run ci:contract",
      "bun run coverage:workflow-suite",
      "bun run lifecycle:invariants",
      "bun run test:critical",
      "- In scope: direct workflow lifecycle automation, state refresh after each operation, zero EXECUTOR lifecycle calls, start/check/evaluate/finalize operations, retries, approvals, waits, human input, and golden scenario metrics.\n- Out of scope: branch_pr provider/PR/merge integration.",
      "1. Map the direct lifecycle onto typed supervisor operations and episode boundaries.\n2. Prepare a role-specific EXECUTOR work order and launch through typed runner results.\n3. Observe process/Git/check/artifact evidence and run the EVALUATOR episode.\n4. Apply safe post-operations until terminal or an approval/wait/human step.\n5. Compare golden-path quality and orchestration cost to the 0.6.24 baseline.",
      "1. Run the approved direct golden task. Expected: EXECUTOR performs zero AgentPlane lifecycle calls; supervisor starts, observes, evaluates, verifies, and finalizes.\n2. Change route state after every operation fixture. Expected: the supervisor recomputes from fresh state and never executes a stale next step.\n3. Exercise approval required, missing knowledge, evaluator rework, out-of-scope write, and adapter crash. Expected: bounded typed stops/retries with no synthesized semantic summary.\n4. Compare baseline metrics. Expected: lifecycle/tool/duplicate-context cost decreases without lower verified success or safety.\n5. Run direct workflow coverage, lifecycle invariants, contract CI, and focused tests."
    ]
  },
